{"v":1,"agent":"codex","cli_version":"dev","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-05-08T18:58:53.361Z","content":[{"text":"**Findings**\n\n- **Medium:** `entire explain --json --session \u003carchived-session\u003e` still misses older sessions in multi-session checkpoints. `runExplainListJSON` filters via `SessionIDs`, but `getBranchCheckpoints` builds `strategy.RewindPoint` without copying `cpInfo.SessionCount` or `cpInfo.SessionIDs`, so production data only exposes the latest `SessionID`. This breaks the new machine-readable list surface for Baton-style lookup by archived session ID. See [explain.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain.go:2169) and [explain_export.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go:543). Add those fields to the `RewindPoint` and cover it with a real multi-session committed checkpoint test.\n\n- **Medium:** SHA-256 rewind transcript restoration is still gated on a 40-character commit hash. In SHA-256 repos, temporary checkpoint commit IDs are 64 chars, so `rewind` skips `restoreSessionTranscriptFromShadow` even when `MetadataDir` is present. The new SHA-256 test verifies init and checkpoint creation, but condenses immediately and does not exercise temporary rewind/transcript restoration. See [rewind.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/rewind.go:337), [rewind.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/rewind.go:540), and [sha256_repo_test.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/sha256_repo_test.go:48). Replace the fixed length check with a hash-shape check that accepts SHA-1 and SHA-256, or key off `MetadataDir`/lack of `CheckpointID`.\n\nI reviewed the committed diff for `issues...HEAD` and ignored unrelated uncommitted worktree changes. I did not run tests.","type":"text"}]}
